<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37862" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπᾰείδω</span></b> , 
			contr.
		
		
			Att.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπᾴδω</span></b> , fut.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ᾴσομαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Ec.</u>
					1153
				</span></i>
			, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ᾴσω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ach.Tat.
					2.7
				</span></i>
			:—<i>sing to</i> or <i>in accompaniment,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μάγος ἀνὴρ . . ἐ. θεογονίην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					1.132
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾠδὰν χορῷ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>El.</u>
					864
				</span></i>
			(lyr.):—
				Pass.
			, <i><span class="en">
				Arr.
				<u>An.</u>
				2.16.3
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>sing as an incantation,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἃ αἱ Σειρῆνες ἐπῇδον τῷ Ὀδυσσεῖ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Mem.</u>
					2.6.11
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χρὴ τὰ τοιαῦτα ὥσπερ ἐπᾴδειν
					ἑαυτῷ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Phd.</u>
					114d
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				77e
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. ἡμῖν αὐτοῖς τοῦτον τὸν λόγον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>R.</u>
					608a
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. τινί</span>
			<i>sing to</i> one <i>so as to charm</i> or <i>soothe</i> him,
				<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Phdr.</u>
				267d
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Lg.</u>
				812c
			</span></i>, al.:—
				Pass.
			, <i><span class="en">
				Porph.
				<u>Chr.</u>
				35
			</span></i>: abs., <i>use charms</i> or <i>incantations,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Tht.</u>
				157c
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπαείδων</span>”
				<i>by means of charms,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					1021
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.), cf. <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				773d
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Tht.</u>
				149d
			</span></i>.</div>
